<title>USA: N.Y. State Housing deal yields 6.10 pct in 2025.</title>
<headline>N.Y. State Housing deal yields 6.10 pct in 2025.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs &amp; Co said Wednesday it tentatively priced $11.5 million New York State Housing Finance Agency refunding bonds at a top yield of 6.10 percent in 2025.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>NEW YORK STATE HOUSING FINANCE AGENCY</p>
<p>RE: $11,480,000*</p>
<p>MULTI-FAMILY MORTGAGE REVENUE REFUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>(FHA INSURED)</p>
<p>1996 SERIES A</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: NAF		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>						EXP</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 05/15/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 11/15</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>11/15/1997		  100M    4.00  %</p>
<p>11/15/1998		  170M    4.30  %</p>
<p>11/15/1999		  175M    4.50  %</p>
<p>11/15/2000		  185M    4.65  %</p>
<p>11/15/2001		  190M    4.75  %</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>11/15/2002		  200M    4.85  %</p>
